      "writtenOn": "2020-06-15T20:35:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am still unclear on how we got into this situation, so the following is tentative:\n\nIIUC, we somehow got past pe_attempt_port_discovery while discovery needed to be done without proceeding to the next step. I believe this would be incorrect behavior, but for the sake of this clause, let\u0027s assume that it\u0027s going to happen sometimes.\n\nAt this point, we don\u0027t want to proceed until both SVIDs and modes are fully discovered. Therefore, this should be something like,\n\npd_get_svids_discovery(port, TCPC_TX_SOP) !\u003d PD_DISC_COMPLETE || pd_get_modes_discovery(port, TCCP_TX_SOP) !\u003d PD_DISC_COMPLETE\n\nRight now, we are only doing DisplayPort, so SOP is sufficient to check. In the general case (Thunderbolt), we would also need to check SOP\u0027.",
